      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no safe way to mitigate this specific drug-herb interaction by just adjusting the dose or timing. The interaction is systemic, meaning the herb affects your body's entire drug metabolism system. Since the risk to your birth control's effectiveness is significant, trying to \"manage\" it yourself is not advisable. To ensure both your mood and your contraception are working as intended, a quick consultation with a pharmacist or your prescribing doctor is the wisest and most straightforward step.",
      "source": "target",
